# L §5.18: "solve may also appear in a def rule that points at a version (v) whose source names the method ... its
# bracket's literals are allowed (§7.1), and its pin of v holds while the rule's value is evaluated".  F(g) = 0.8 g -
# 800 on [0, 2000], u = 1: m = 0 + floor(2000/2) = 1000, F(1000) = 0: the answer is 1000.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source glaw "gross-up law"
input g: num
input keep: num
input target: num
def netx: num = g * keep at reader
def grossed: num at reader
  rule r v gu = solve netx == target for g in [0, 2000] to 1

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  g = 1
  keep = 0.8
  target = 800
version gu
  cite glaw
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01

ask a: grossed law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: 1 000
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
